received the Ph.D. degree in 2025 from the Department of Electrical, Computer, and Systems Engineering at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, Troy, NY, USA. His doctoral research focused on efficient data management over computational storage. He received the M.S. and B.S. degree in Electrical Engineering from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
